      "writtenOn": "2022-05-02T11:23:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A headset might disconnect from the Android device by itself, causing it to be removed automatically. Even without handling the grouped reconnection case, could we check when mCallbacks.notifySourceRemoved() is called and make sure we remove source from mGroupOpDevices when all members of the same group are disconnected?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 923,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 923,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "33b49b2015c8944483d4201dc894574deb961070",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0426ff0b_80992a7e",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/bass_client/BassClientService.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 923,
      "author": {
        "id": 1928988
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-04T10:08:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure if I got it right. Let me clarify on how this patch works. `mGroupOpDevices` is not holding any broadcast source devices but the sink devices (BASS servers). We bind the group trigger flag with the sink device, so that when the client app is triggering an action on that sink, we could trigger it on other group members that this device is part of. The group operation trigger flag sticks only to the device that was used in `addSource()` call, with `isGroupOp` set to true (we can call it a Lead Device). That means if the app calls `removeSource()` not on the lead device but the other group member, the operation will not be performed on the group, but the single device only.\n\n`mCallbacks.notifySourceRemoved()` seems to be called only from one place in the state machine, and probably we should remove the sticky flag from the device if the device decides to remove the broadcast source on its own. I did that in the latest patch revision.",
      "parentUuid": "8f3390e3_ae42d1cb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 923,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 923,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "33b49b2015c8944483d4201dc894574deb961070",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "96aff3e1_fb2ffa67",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/bass_client/BassClientService.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 923,
      "author": {
        "id": 1929540
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-04T11:43:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "two cents from my side:\n\n1) I think all the devices in the group should have sticky flag. If one gots disconnected, then operations on other device in the group should be still in the group context\n\n2) If device disconnects (ACL is disconnected) it does not imply that Source has been removed. Peer device still might be sync to the broadcast. \n\n3) If remote device autonomously removes the \"Source\" I think we should respect it, but do not remove the sticky flag as long as the User did not call Remove Source.\n\n4) Do we allow user to add more than 1 source? If so, then instead of flag we should have reference counter, or keep flag as long as all the group devices got disconnected.",
      "parentUuid": "0426ff0b_80992a7e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 923,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 923,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "33b49b2015c8944483d4201dc894574deb961070",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
